          "solution": "**Step 1: Set up the generator line through an arbitrary point**  \nLet $P(x, y, z)$ be an arbitrary point on the cylinder. The generators have direction ratios $(l, m, n) = (1, 2, 3)$.\n\nThe equations of the generator line passing through $P(x, y, z)$ are:\n$$\\frac{X - x}{1} = \\frac{Y - y}{2} = \\frac{Z - z}{3}$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Find the point of intersection with $Z = 0$**  \nSetting $Z = 0$:\n$$\\frac{X - x}{1} = \\frac{Y - y}{2} = \\frac{-z}{3}$$\n\nSolving for $X$ and $Y$:\n$$X = x - \\frac{z}{3}$$\n$$Y = y - \\frac{2z}{3}$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Impose the guiding curve condition**  \nThe intersection point $(X, Y, 0)$ must satisfy the ellipse equation $X^2 + 2Y^2 = 1$:\n$$\\left(x - \\frac{z}{3}\\right)^2 + 2\\left(y - \\frac{2z}{3}\\right)^2 = 1$$\n\nExpanding:\n$$\\left(\\frac{3x - z}{3}\\right)^2 + 2\\left(\\frac{3y - 2z}{3}\\right)^2 = 1$$\n$$\\frac{(3x - z)^2}{9} + \\frac{2(3y - 2z)^2}{9} = 1$$\n\nMultiply through by 9:\n$$(3x - z)^2 + 2(3y - 2z)^2 = 9$$\n\nExpanding each squared term:\n$$(9x^2 - 6xz + z^2) + 2(9y^2 - 12yz + 4z^2) = 9$$\n$$9x^2 + 18y^2 + z^2 + 8z^2 - 6xz - 24yz = 9$$\n$$9x^2 + 18y^2 + 9z^2 - 6xz - 24yz - 9 = 0$$\n\nDividing the entire equation by 3:\n$$3x^2 + 6y^2 + 3z^2 - 2xz - 8yz - 3 = 0$$\n\nThis is the exact Cartesian equation of the cylinder."
