          "tier": 3,
          "title": "Enveloping Cone of a Sphere: Derivation and Exact Form",
          "statement": "Find the equation of the enveloping cone of the sphere:\n$$S: x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 2x + 4y = 1$$\nwith vertex at the external point $V(1, 1, 1)$. Verify that the vertex satisfies the tangency envelope condition.",
          "solution": "**Step 1: Write the sphere equation and compute $S_1$ and $T$**  \nThe sphere is $S(x, y, z) = x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 2x + 4y - 1 = 0$.\n\nFor vertex $V(x_1, y_1, z_1) = (1, 1, 1)$:\n$$S_1 = S(1, 1, 1) = 1^2 + 1^2 + 1^2 - 2(1) + 4(1) - 1 = 3 - 2 + 4 - 1 = 4$$\n\nNow evaluate the tangent form $T(x, y, z)$:\n$$T = x x_1 + y y_1 + z z_1 - (x + x_1) + 2(y + y_1) - 1$$\nSubstitute $x_1 = 1, y_1 = 1, z_1 = 1$:\n$$T = x(1) + y(1) + z(1) - (x + 1) + 2(y + 1) - 1$$\n$$T = x + y + z - x - 1 + 2y + 2 - 1 = 3y + z$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 2: Apply the Joachimsthal Envelope Formula $S S_1 = T^2$**  \n$$S \\cdot S_1 = T^2$$\n$$(x^2 + y^2 + z^2 - 2x + 4y - 1)(4) = (3y + z)^2$$\n\nExpand both sides:\n$$\\text{LHS} = 4x^2 + 4y^2 + 4z^2 - 8x + 16y - 4$$\n$$\\text{RHS} = 9y^2 + 6yz + z^2$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 3: Collect all terms on one side**  \n$$4x^2 + (4 - 9)y^2 + (4 - 1)z^2 - 6yz - 8x + 16y - 4 = 0$$\n$$4x^2 - 5y^2 + 3z^2 - 6yz - 8x + 16y - 4 = 0$$\n\n---\n\n**Step 4: Verification of Vertex**  \nCheck if $V(1, 1, 1)$ lies on this quadric:\n$$4(1)^2 - 5(1)^2 + 3(1)^2 - 6(1)(1) - 8(1) + 16(1) - 4$$\n$$= 4 - 5 + 3 - 6 - 8 + 16 - 4 = 23 - 23 = 0 \\quad \\checkmark$$\n\nThus, the equation of the enveloping cone is:\n$$4x^2 - 5y^2 + 3z^2 - 6yz - 8x + 16y - 4 = 0$$"
